flowchart TB
  accTitle: Detaching from Herdr versus restarting its server
  accDescr: Detaching or losing SSH leaves original processes running while the background server and host stay alive and awake. A server stop or host reboot ends those processes. A later start restores layout and eligible native agent conversations.

  run["Herdr background session<br/>Panes and tasks running"]
  detach["Detach / disconnect SSH<br/>Ctrl+B → q"]
  live["Server alive, host awake<br/>Original processes continue"]
  attach["Reconnect<br/>herdr returns to the live session"]
  stop["Server stop / host reboot<br/>Original processes end"]
  restore["Start Herdr again<br/>Restore layout and directories"]
  eligible["Eligible agents<br/>Resume integrated native sessions"]
  manual["Other commands and panes<br/>New shells; rerun tasks as needed"]
  run --> detach --> live --> attach
  run --> stop --> restore
  restore --> eligible
  restore --> manual
